commit c9bc4af270337679ebf96f4fefb32c5255d728c2
Author: María <mariagrandury@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 22 08:52:13 2026 +0200

    evals+analysis: the reformulated twins become ordinary benchmarks
    
    groups.auto in configs/tasks.json gains rf_belebele, rf_global_mmlu_full,
    rf_include_base_44 and rfgm_include_base_44, and the 43
    rfgm_include_base_44_* tasks are registered with their YAMLs.
    
    One config change does three jobs. auto_evals_cscs.py reads this group and
    is per-task idempotent, so every evaluated checkpoint is topped up with only
    its missing tasks rather than re-run. utils.trained_only resolves through
    auto_benchmarks(), so rule 2 stops deleting every rf_* row - 46,921 of them,
    124 distinct tasks, dropped before any analysis saw them. And above_random.py
    calls the same helper, which is why rf rows carried population=all while
    their originals carried trained: the twins were gated on a different
    population from the benchmarks they are compared against. They now split
    124 trained / 61 all, matching the originals' 324/138.
    
    make_rf_tasks.py gains --family, so a family still mid-rewrite is not
    registered with a partial item set; without it, registering rfgm would have
    picked up belebele_deu_Latn at 289 of its 900 rows. It also stops discarding
    a twin's derived n_items when the entry is rewritten: the gate needs that
    count, and a re-run would have dropped all 185 rf_ tasks out of the gate
    silently. Both sets now regenerate byte-identically.
    
    grids.display() renders rf_belebele as "belebele-rf" and sorts a twin beside
    its original. rq09's FAMILY_META gains six entries carrying two new format
    values, cloze_completion and statement_continuation.
    
    rewrite_items_gemini.py names the missing export when
    GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI is unset, instead of dying six frames down in the
    SDK with "No API key was provided" - two belebele launches were lost to it.
    
    RULES.md records that the populations moved (rule 13) and that a twin
    re-measures its original's items, so it is not an independent task for
    rule 8.

